<article class="env-lemma" id="06E3">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/06E3">Lemma <span data-tag="06E3">79.9.7</span>.</a> In Situation <a href="/tag/06DY" data-tag="06DY">79.9.2</a>. If $r : \mathop{\mathrm{Spec}}(k) \to R$ is a morphism such that $s \circ r, t \circ r$ are automorphisms of $\mathop{\mathrm{Spec}}(k)$, then the map </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  R \longrightarrow R, \quad x \longmapsto c(r, x)  \]
</div>
  <p> is an automorphism $R \to R$ which maps $e$ to $r$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Proof is identical to the proof of More on Groupoids, Lemma <a href="/tag/04LS" data-tag="04LS">40.10.6</a>. 
